This implies $k$ must be a divisor of $n$. If $n$ is not divisible by $k$, we can't partition the boxes perfectly into groups of size $k$. So we only care about $k$ such that $n \% k == 0$.

Let $m = n/k$ be the number of trucks.
The weights of the trucks are sums of contiguous subarrays of length $k$.
