The weight of the $j$-th truck (1-indexed) is $P_{jk} - P_{(j-1)k}$.
We need to find $\max_{j} (P_{jk} - P_{(j-1)k}) - \min_{j} (P_{jk} - P_{(j-1)k})$.

Since $n$ can be up to $150,000$, iterating over all divisors $k$ is efficient enough because the sum of divisors is not too large, but actually we just need to iterate over all $k$ that divide $n$. The number of divisors can be large for highly composite numbers, but for $n \le 150,000$, the maximum number of divisors is 160 (for 144000 or similar). So iterating over divisors is very fast.

